<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emil Constantinescu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1939</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emil Constantinescu is a Romanian geologist and politician who served as president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a> from 1996 to 2000. Candidate of the centre-right Romanian Democratic Convention, he defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ion-iliescu">Ion Iliescu</a> in 1996, the first peaceful transfer of power to the opposition since the fall of communism. His term saw economic hardship and steps towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a> and EU membership.</p></div>
